{"id":"n-20261008-o3ndde","category":"sports","display_title":"Maccabi Haifa Returns Teddy Tickets","display_title_he":"מכבי חיפה מחזירה את הכרטיסים לטדי","short_summary":"Maccabi Haifa returned all ticket invitations for their match at Teddy Stadium against Hapoel Jerusalem, citing safety concerns and alleged police violence.","english_level":"C1","words":417,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/israelisoccer/article/h1db704ifg","title":"מכבי חיפה נגד הפועל ירושלים: \"לא מרגישים בטוחים בטדי\"","published_at":"2026-10-08T08:29:23.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3871373","title":"מכבי חיפה במתקפה על הפועל ירושלים: \"לא מרגישים בטוחים בטדי\"","published_at":"2026-10-08T10:44:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-08T08:29:23.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-08T13:46:25.032Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["A simmering controversy surrounding ticket distributions for the upcoming football fixture between Hapoel Jerusalem and Maccabi Haifa escalated significantly on Thursday morning. The green club from Haifa announced a drastic measure, clarifying that they have returned their entire quota of complimentary invitations for the match at Teddy Stadium and will not utilize them whatsoever. According to official statements released by the visitors, this action was taken in direct response to what they describe as a deeply unsafe environment for visiting supporters, preventing them from feeling secure at the Jerusalem venue.","League regulations stipulate that an away team automatically receives fifty invitations for the visitor section and an additional thirty for the VIP tribune. Maccabi Haifa explained that while their ticketing department received this allocation automatically through standard procedures, they decided to return every single pass. Consequently, even the players' families will not attend the fixture as invited guests. Club representatives heavily emphasized that neither players' relatives nor officials feel secure enough to visit the stadium, pointing directly to ongoing protests regarding severe police violence and challenging stadium conditions that completely fail to guarantee safe passage for supporters.","Furthermore, Maccabi Haifa directed remarkably sharp criticism toward Hapoel Jerusalem's chief executive officer, Uri Schatzky. The management from Haifa asserted that instead of attempting to make provocative remarks to the media, Schatzky should instead conduct a thorough internal review to determine how visiting football fans can reach Teddy Stadium securely without fearing physical harm or violence.","Uri Schatzky, however, quickly contested these claims and urged everyone to stick strictly to the factual reality of the situation. The Hapoel Jerusalem CEO maintained that the ticket invitations were not merely processed through automated systems without the club's active involvement; rather, Maccabi Haifa's management had explicitly requested both the tickets and accompanying parking passes via WhatsApp messages. Schatzky argued vigorously that the visiting club only decided to waive the tickets after the controversy leaked to the public eye. He expressed his sincere hope that Maccabi Haifa supporters would ultimately decide whether or not to attend of their own free will, rather than bowing to rigid directives from their club's leadership, which had initially sought the passes and parking permits.","Addressing the suggestion to examine internal safety practices, Schatzky swiftly dismissed the criticism by pointing out that Maccabi Haifa has more than enough unresolved friction with local police forces in Haifa regarding the treatment of their own fans. He strongly advised them to concentrate on solving their own local problems rather than lecturing others."],"facts":[{"fact":"Maccabi Haifa returned their entire quota of invitations for the upcoming match against Hapoel Jerusalem at Teddy Stadium, stating they do not feel safe there.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The returned quota consists of 50 invitations for the away section and 30 for the VIP section, allocated automatically according to league regulations.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Maccabi Haifa stated that players' families will also not attend the match due to safety concerns and allegations of police violence and inadequate conditions at the venue.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Maccabi Haifa criticized Hapoel Jerusalem CEO Uri Schatzky, telling him to focus on ensuring visiting fans can attend safely rather than making remarks in the media.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Uri Schatzky responded by stating that Maccabi Haifa management explicitly requested the tickets and parking passes via WhatsApp, and only returned them after the issue became public.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Schatzky also suggested that Maccabi Haifa should focus on their own issues with police treatment of their fans in Haifa instead of telling Hapoel Jerusalem to examine its practices.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"simmering","lemma":"simmering","pos":"adjective","he":"מבעבע, מתוח","name":false},{"text":"controversy","lemma":"controversy","pos":"noun","he":"מחלוקת","name":false},{"text":"surrounding","lemma":"surround","pos":"verb","he":"הקשור ל-, סביב","name":false},{"text":"ticket distributions","lemma":"ticket distribution","pos":"noun","he":"חלוקת כרטיסים","name":false},{"text":"upcoming","lemma":"upcoming","pos":"adjective","he":"הקרוב","name":false},{"text":"football fixture","lemma":"football fixture","pos":"noun","he":"משחק כדורגל","name":false},{"text":"between","lemma":"between","pos":"preposition","he":"בין","name":false},{"text":"Hapoel Jerusalem","lemma":"Hapoel Jerusalem","pos":"proper noun","he":"הפועל ירושלים","name":true},{"text":"Maccabi Haifa","lemma":"Maccabi Haifa","pos":"proper noun","he":"מכבי חיפה","name":true},{"text":"escalated","lemma":"escalate","pos":"verb","he":"הסלים","name":false},{"text":"significantly","lemma":"significantly","pos":"adverb","he":"משמעותית","name":false},{"text":"Thursday morning","lemma":"Thursday morning","pos":"noun","he":"בוקר חמישי","name":false},{"text":"green club","lemma":"green club","pos":"noun","he":"המועדון הירוק","name":false},{"text":"announced","lemma":"announce","pos":"verb","he":"הכריז","name":false},{"text":"drastic measure","lemma":"drastic measure","pos":"noun","he":"צעד דרסטי","name":false},{"text":"clarifying","lemma":"clarify","pos":"verb","he":"ובהבהירם","name":false},{"text":"returned","lemma":"return","pos":"verb","he":"החזירו","name":false},{"text":"entire quota","lemma":"entire quota","pos":"noun","he":"מלוא המכסה","name":false},{"text":"complimentary invitations","lemma":"complimentary invitation","pos":"noun","he":"הזמנות חינם","name":false},{"text":"match","lemma":"match","pos":"noun","he":"משחק","name":false},{"text":"Teddy Stadium","lemma":"Teddy Stadium","pos":"proper noun","he":"אצטדיון טדי","name":true},{"text":"utilize","lemma":"utilize","pos":"verb","he":"להשתמש","name":false},{"text":"whatsoever","lemma":"whatsoever","pos":"adverb","he":"בכלל","name":false},{"text":"official statements","lemma":"official statement","pos":"noun","he":"הודעות רשמיות","name":false},{"text":"visitors","lemma":"visitor","pos":"noun","he":"אורחים","name":false},{"text":"action","lemma":"action","pos":"noun","he":"פעולה","name":false},{"text":"direct response","lemma":"direct response","pos":"noun","he":"תגובה ישירה","name":false},{"text":"deeply unsafe environment","lemma":"deeply unsafe environment","pos":"noun","he":"סביבה לא בטוחה בעליל","name":false},{"text":"visiting supporters","lemma":"visiting supporter","pos":"noun","he":"אוהדים אורחים","name":false},{"text":"preventing","lemma":"prevent","pos":"verb","he":"מונע","name":false},{"text":"feeling secure","lemma":"feel secure","pos":"verb","he":"להרגיש בטוחים","